From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: add the HY300 T08 board dts

The HY300 T08 (issue #7; silkscreen HY300_T08_QZ713_V3, DDR3 at 640 MHz,
a 1280x720 single-port panel at project 0x34, "ADT-3 2024" display
firmware) gets a device tree of its own, so that the DTB a TEST image for
it boots is named after this board.

Its owner's stock device tree (the boot package of his eMMC dump,
01.11.2026) is the HY300 Pro's for everything on the board: the LEDs, the
fan with its tacho on PH17, the focus motor on PH4..PH7 with the HY300
Pro's tables and limiter PH14, the lamp's PWM channel 5 (panel_config.ini
[PWMSetting]: channel 5, polarity 1, 40 kHz, vsync lock 1, duty 1..100,
as on the HY300 Pro), the Wi-Fi and Bluetooth lines, the accelerometer
node on twi1, the codec. It differs from the HY300 Pro's in three places,
none of which reaches this tree: the focus motor's timing (the HY300
Pro's values are what this tree carries already), a smaller decoder
reservation (ours is the larger one), and a 150 MHz SDIO clock (ours is
capped at 25 MHz). Its stock tree also switches on an eight-key LRADC
keyboard; the owner checked the case: the power button is the only key,
getevent on the stock system reports KEY_POWER and nothing else. So no
keyboard node, the power key stays PL4 as on the HY300 Pro.

What is not the HY300 Pro's is the display firmware: the T08 runs the
"ADT-3 2024" display.bin (22a7df11...) of the HY350 and the HY320, not the
HY300 Pro's. The two values the HY320 measured for that firmware (0335)
come along: the elog ring and control block the firmware writes
(<0x4b48ae00 0x4b271d9c> in ARM view), and the AFBD handoff words the
firmware leaves after the logo (CTRL 0x03001901, VIDEO_CTRL 0x03000200,
selector 0). The HY320's mix window (0340) is not named here: whether this
board's panel block needs it is not known, and without the "mix" resource
the driver writes nothing.

Wi-Fi is an AIC8801 (SDIO 5449:0145), not the AIC8800D80; the driver
tells the chips apart itself, the tree says nothing about it.

Nothing on this board has been measured by us, and it has no serial
console; its owner has no remote either, so a TEST image can only be
reached over Wi-Fi. Built (dtc, against the series applied to 6.18.38);
not booted.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy310.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-l018.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy320.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-t08.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-h728-x96qpro+.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-t527-avaota-a1.dtb
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-t08.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-t08.dts
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-t08.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+/*
+ * MagCubic HY300 T08 projector (silkscreen HY300_T08_QZ713_V3; issue #7).
+ * Stock Android 10 of the ADT-3 vendor build 6245789; DDR3 at 640 MHz;
+ * 1280x720 single-port panel, project 0x34; "ADT-3 2024" display firmware.
+ *
+ * The HY300 Pro's tree: its owner's stock device tree (boot package of his
+ * eMMC dump, 01.11.2026) agrees with the HY300 Pro's on every pin and every
+ * table of the board - LEDs, fan and tacho PH17, focus motor PH4..PH7 with
+ * the HY300 Pro's timing and limiter PH14, lamp PWM 5, Wi-Fi/BT lines, the
+ * accelerometer on twi1, the codec. The eight-key LRADC keyboard its stock
+ * tree enables is firmware heritage: the case has the power button only
+ * (owner, getevent: KEY_POWER and nothing else), so no keyboard node here.
+ *
+ * What differs is the display firmware: the "ADT-3 2024" display.bin of
+ * the HY350 and HY320, not the HY300 Pro's. Its elog addresses and its
+ * AFBD handoff words are the ones the HY320 measured (0335). The HY320's
+ * mix window is not named: not known to be needed here; without the "mix"
+ * resource the AFBD driver writes nothing.
+ *
+ * Wi-Fi: an AIC8801, which the driver tells apart itself. Nothing on this
+ * board has been measured by us; it has no serial console, and its owner
+ * has no remote. The image built from this is a TEST image for its owner.
+ */
+
+#include "sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "MagCubic HY300 T08";
+	compatible = "magcubic,hy300-t08", "allwinner,sun50i-h713";
+};
+
+/* the "ADT-3 2024" firmware's elog ring and control block (0335, HY320) */
+&cpu_comm {
+	allwinner,elog = <0x4b48ae00 0x4b271d9c>;
+};
+
+/*
+ * What that firmware leaves in the AFBD after the logo (0335, HY320): CTRL,
+ * VIDEO_CTRL, selector. With the HY310's defaults the driver refused.
+ */
+&display {
+	allwinner,handoff-state = <0x03001901 0x03000200 0x00000000>;
+};
